.TH G-UNITY7-CLEANUP 8 "November 2026" "g-unity7-desktop" "G Unity7"
.SH NAME
g-unity7-cleanup \- let apt autoremove the packages of Ubuntu Unity that G Unity7 does not use
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B g-unity7-cleanup
.RB [ \-n | \-\-dry\-run ]
.RB [ \-y | \-\-yes ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
The installer of Ubuntu Unity installs the
.B ubuntu-unity-desktop
task and apt marks its packages as manually installed, so
.B apt autoremove
never removes them.
.B g-unity7-cleanup
marks
.B ubuntu-unity-desktop
and the manually installed packages of the task that
.B g-unity7-desktop
does not depend on, recommend or suggest as automatically installed.
It shows the packages and what
.B apt \-\-purge autoremove
will remove then, and asks for confirmation.
A marked package that is still needed by another package is kept by autoremove.
.PP
Run
.B sudo apt \-\-purge autoremove
afterwards to remove the packages. To keep one of them, mark it as manually
installed first:
.BI "sudo apt-mark manual " package
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-dry\-run
Only show the packages, change nothing. It does not need root.
.TP
.BR \-y ", " \-\-yes
Do not ask for confirmation.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR apt (8),
.BR apt-mark (8)
